---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import ScreenFrame from '../../components/screens/ScreenFrame.astro';
import PresetScreen from '../../components/screens/PresetScreen.astro';
import EditScreen from '../../components/screens/EditScreen.astro';
import EqScreen from '../../components/screens/EqScreen.astro';
import TunerScreen from '../../components/screens/TunerScreen.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/url';
---

<DocsLayout
  title="UI & Controls"
  description="Use the Ardor touchscreen, four footswitches, and encoder to choose sounds, edit a chain, and tune."
  lede="The Ardor screen is made for playing. Choose a preset with your foot, change a sound on the touch display, and keep the signal path easy to follow from left to right."
>
  <h2>Preset screen</h2>
  <ScreenFrame label="Preset" caption="The home screen: four slots in the active bank.">
    <PresetScreen />
  </ScreenFrame>
  <p>The home screen shows four preset slots and these controls:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Bank −/+</strong> moves between banks.</li>
    <li><strong>Tuner</strong> opens the chromatic tuner.</li>
    <li><strong>Edit</strong> opens the signal path editor.</li>
    <li><strong>Settings</strong> opens Wi-Fi and display settings.</li>
    <li>The footer shows the master volume and audio status.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Edit a sound</h2>
  <ScreenFrame label="Edit" caption="The signal moves in one horizontal path from input to output.">
    <EditScreen />
  </ScreenFrame>
  <p>
    The editor shows the signal from left to right. Your guitar enters at the left. Each
    effect appears in the order that it runs. The output is at the right. Scroll the canvas
    sideways when a chain is longer than the screen.
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>Tap <strong>+</strong> between two blocks to add an effect.</li>
    <li>Tap a block to open its controls.</li>
    <li>Drag a block to change its place in the chain.</li>
    <li>Use the filter buttons to find amps, cabinets, delays, reverbs, and other effects.</li>
    <li>Tap <strong>Save</strong> when you want to keep the change.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Tap <strong>Split Left / Right</strong> when you want two horizontal paths. See{' '}
    <a href={url('/docs/dual-rig')}>the Dual Rig &amp; Dual Amp</a> guide for the two-path layout.
  </p>

  <h2>Change effect controls</h2>
  <ScreenFrame label="EQ" caption="The five-band EQ shows the tone shape on a live graph.">
    <EqScreen />
  </ScreenFrame>
  <p>
    Most effects show large sliders with the control name and value. Drag a slider, or tap
    its value when the control supports direct entry. Use the bypass control to hear the
    sound with the effect off. The five-band EQ has a separate page with a live graph.
  </p>

  <h2>Tuner</h2>
  <ScreenFrame label="Tuner" caption="The tuner mutes the output while you tune.">
    <TunerScreen />
  </ScreenFrame>
  <p>
    The tuner shows the note, frequency, and whether the note is flat or sharp. It mutes the
    output while it is open. Tap the on-screen exit button, or press any footswitch, to
    leave the tuner.
  </p>

  <h2>Footswitches and encoder</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Control</th><th>Action</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td class="mono">Footswitch 1–4</td><td>Choose preset slots 1–4 in the active bank.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="mono">Encoder</td><td>Change the master output volume.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="mono">Hold FS1 + FS2</td><td>Hold for one second to mute and open the tuner.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Any footswitch</td><td>Leave the tuner without changing the preset.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      If you change the preset or bank with unsaved edits, Ardor asks whether to{' '}
      <strong>Save</strong>,
      <strong>Discard</strong>, or <strong>Cancel</strong>. Your draft
      does not disappear without a choice.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    You can also control presets and effect parameters with MIDI or an expression pedal. See
    the <a href={url('/docs/hardware')}>Hardware guide</a> for the optional connections.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
